@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+# Negotiated compaction lifecycle
+
+ACP v1 clients opt in with `clientCapabilities.session.compaction: {}`. The
+adapter uses the SDK 1.4.0 public `session/update` union. Unsupported, null, or
+malformed capabilities retain synthetic tool updates and the deprecated text
+banner. No compaction summaries are forwarded on the negotiated path.
+
+Native item IDs become compaction IDs, including terminal-only history replay.
+The deprecated `thread/compacted` banner is suppressed for opted-in clients;
+that ID-less event cannot be joined reliably to a native item. Genuine tool
+updates without the adapter's context-compaction metadata remain tools.
+
+The proposed `agentCapabilities._meta["ai.ours/compactionSafety"]` advertises
+`version: 1`, `lifecycle: "completion_only"`, and `guardedCancel: false`.
+Observed starts are forwarded, but complete start/failure/cancellation coverage
+is not established. Missing terminals after stream loss or turn failure are
+unknown outcomes, never synthesized success. Consumers must wait for prompt
+settlement and reconcile unresolved starts; no lifecycle event permits automatic
+cancellation.
+
+## Outcome evidence and limits
+
+This patch targets adapter commit `effb0fe670a49dfbb5071764b5f8a2e3c09e2393`
+(package 1.11.0), whose lockfile selects native Codex 0.153.4. At native commit
+`3d2ee51ca2d5db578f328aa75e20aa22c0197c9a` (tag `rust-v0.153.4`):
+
+- `codex-rs/core/src/compact.rs:379-394` awaits history replacement and token
+  recomputation before emitting the context-compaction item completed event.
+- `codex-rs/core/src/compact_remote.rs:295-310` does the same; unsuccessful remote
+  attempts return earlier without this completion.
+
+Thus these item completions represent installed compacted history; a later
+post-compaction hook can still stop the enclosing turn. This is not proof of
+complete runtime coverage, durable filesystem persistence, or equivalent
+semantics in an overridden runtime binary. Deterministic tests cover the
+adapter mapping and SDK v1 wire negotiation, not paid live compaction or v2.
